{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>So I turned and came down from the mountain</b>. I have already explained in its place (ibid. 11) that before he descended from the mountain he prayed on their behalf, and during his prayer it is stated (ibid. 14), <i>and HaShem relented from the evil</i>. But he does not mention this now, because he wishes to set before them now the great burden and the toil that he burdened upon them: that he brought them to the breaking of the tablets, and to falling upon them forty days and forty nights, and to praying also on behalf of Aaron, for HaShem was very incensed with him. And afterwards (Deuteronomy 9:25–29) he mentions the first prayer, with which he entreated the face of HaShem his Elohim, before his descent, that He not destroy them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:47:13.236355458Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}